## Context

Filed from the project climate-finance-het by the session that landed its
PRs 2167 and 2185 on 2026-11-13 (host padme). Both reviews hit the same
behaviour of `scripts/touched-tests.py`; one of them could not complete.

## What happened

- **Gaze on PR 2185** (head fa21414d, review `rv-20261113-pr-2185-a173`,
  answer `20261113T124439325Z-padme-ff93c925`). The tests item printed
  `fallback: full integration tier`, because no test names the table builder
  `docs/reports/t3104-r0-abstract-table-2026-11-13.py` or
  `scripts/catalog_rel_r0_service_abstracts.py`. The run hit the 300 s cap
  and filed no report: plan check FAIL, result ESCALATE, with no finding in
  hand. Verify-gate then refused the PR ("no completed review"). Before the
  cap the run printed 2 failures, both `torch.OutOfMemoryError` in
  `tests/test_divergence.py`, code the PR does not touch.
- **Verify-gate on PR 2167** (verdict `20261113T130636896Z-padme-e2974783`).
  The diff holds one Python file, `docs/reports/t3018-gate-removal-2026-11-13.py`,
  a report generator no test imports. The gate printed `selected: none`,
  the same fallback, and `result: fail`: 9 failed, 558 passed, 1 skipped,
  about 11 of the gate's 17 minutes. All 9 failures are CUDA out-of-memory
  on the RTX 5070 Ti, which another process held. The gate reran the 9 on
  the card the project's make targets select (RTX A4000): all pass. It
  ruled APPROVED by reading the failure as environmental.

## Observations

- `scripts/touched-tests.py:168` runs `pytest -m integration tests/`
  directly. The project selects its test device in its Makefile
  (`GATE_DEV`, from `scripts/qa_gate_gpu.py`: `CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID`
  and the card with most free memory, else CPU under `nice -n 19`), so the
  selection applies only to runs started through `make`. A direct pytest
  run takes torch's default `cuda:0`, the card the LLM service holds.
- A Python file under `docs/reports/` counts as a changed source file. The
  project's own gate for such a diff is `make lint` and `make check-fast`
  (plus `make check-domain-rel` when a domain test changes); all three
  passed on both heads. The integration tier is not part of it.
- Cause of the 300 s overrun not isolated: the tier ran in about 11 minutes
  in the gate, on a host that was also running other sessions' tests.

## Exit criteria

Amended 2026-11-13 on the author's acceptance of
`design/2026-11-13-touched-tests-fallback.md`: the device criterion moved to
climate-finance-het, where the device selection lives (its ticket 3128, its
PR 2198). The original three criteria are in this file's git history.

- [x] A review whose fallback tier outruns the reviewer's budget does not end
      ESCALATE for want of a report: `touched-tests.py --integration-timeout`
      stops the tier and prints `result: incomplete`, and gaze's tests item
      passes that bound (`skills/gaze/references/panel.md`).
- [x] A regression test reproduces the case before the fix
      (`tests/test_touched_tests.py`, the tier that outruns its bound).
- [x] The out-of-memory false alarms are handed to the project: ticket 3128
      of climate-finance-het is filed (PR 2198 there).

Later review, 2026-11-27: the recount of the note's § 6, step 3.
